        <div id="short-answer" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>The Short Answer</h2>
<p>
            <strong>A curved treadmill costs about $1,100 to $4,500 for a real slatted home trainer, with most popular
            models between $1,900 and $3,500 (makers&rsquo; stores and Amazon, 23 November 2026). Premium and club models
            run from about $6,000 to over $15,000, and &ldquo;curved&rdquo; machines under $1,000 are walking pads with a
            rubber belt, not sprint trainers.</strong> There is no electricity bill and no subscription, so the sticker
            price is most of what you pay.
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Curved walking pads:</strong> $679.99 to $799.99 on Amazon (JOROTO, ERGOLIFE, Rongle). Walking and light jogging only.</li>
            <li><strong>Entry slatted trainers:</strong> $1,095 to about $1,600 (SB Fitness CT250 and CT400, Sunny SF-X7140).</li>
            <li><strong>The home sweet spot:</strong> $1,895 to $2,799 (SB Fitness CT550, Sole C80 at $2,099.99, SB Fitness CT700, AssaultRunner Classic).</li>
            <li><strong>Premium:</strong> $2,995 to $4,600 (AssaultRunner Pro $3,499, TrueForm Trainer $3,495, Woodway Curve LTG $3,495, AssaultRunner Elite $4,499).</li>
            <li><strong>Top end:</strong> $6,195 to $9,195 for a TrueForm Runner, from $8,199 for a NOHrD Sprintbok.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            For what a curved treadmill does and does not do well, read our <a href="/curved-treadmill-guide/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">curved treadmill guide</a>; for the
            machines we would shortlist, see the <a href="/best-curved-treadmills/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">best curved treadmills</a>. One of the dearest, the motorless <a href="/centr-treadmills/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">Centr x HYROX Perform Tread</a> from Chris Hemsworth’s brand, is $6,999.
          </p>
        </div>

